  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday Night through Friday)\nIssued at 1049 PM CDT Fri Oct 16 2026\n\nBy Saturday night, the surface ridge axis will have shifted east\nand will lie from the Ozarks back into far eastern OK. Conditions\nappear favorable again toward daybreak Sunday morning for patchy\nfrost in the valleys of NW AR and far NE OK.\n\nA steady warming trend is forecast next week, with ridging aloft\nprevailing over the central part of the country. Highs return to\nthe 80s again by Wednesday and rise to the mid 80s toward the end\nof the week.\n\nAn upper trough is expected to develop near the West Coast early\nnext week but will take its time moving east toward the Plains.\nCurrent expectations are for a dry forecast next week with low \nrain chances by next weekend.\n\nLacy",
